closest-possible: Crystal builds the text as a String in prepare, then each run splits it on spaces and counts with Hash(String, Int32). The port stores the text as list<byte, 400000> (the generator's letters are bytes, not a String), scans it by hand for spaces instead of split(' '), and counts with map<Ascii max 8, int, 65536> plus parallel first-seen lists instead of a Hash. Each word is rebuilt from bytes every run, as Crystal's split does. Word order and tie-breaking match: first-seen order plus strict > equals Crystal's Hash insertion order with max_by's first-maximal result. The word cap of 8 letters is exact for word_len 4 (max 3+2+3 = 8). Prep split: prep mode runs the untimed text generation plus the warmup rounds, matching Crystal's prepare plus warmup; Crystal's prepare has no timed work, so prep ends after warmup.
